    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d127">

                <pb facs="0212" n="96" sameAs="frus:frus1912/pg96"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 893.51/416.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The American Ambassador to Japan to the Secretary of
                        State</hi>.</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.—Extract.—Paraphrase.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">American Embassy</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Tokyo</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1911-05-13">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">May 13, 1911</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>The Minister for Foreign Affairs today inquired whether participation if granted
                    would place Japan in a position superior to an ordinary bondholder. He said that
                    Japan is greatly concerned in the Chinese currency reform, especially as to the
                    purposes of the Manchurian allotment.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">O’Brien</hi>.</signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
